    {
      "id": "plotpoint",
      "zh": "转折点",
      "en": "Plot point",
      "zh_alt": "情节点",
      "category": "narrative",
      "module": "故事创作",
      "def_zh": "勾住剧情、把它转往另一个方向的事件。常用的有激励事件、大转折一（情节点一）、中点、大转折二（情节点二）、高潮；连续剧按季安排。",
      "def_en": "An event that hooks into the action and spins the story in another direction (Syd Field). The common set: inciting incident, plot point one, midpoint, plot point two, climax; in a series they are scheduled per season.",
      "where": "1.1.1 故事结构、1.1.2.2 连续剧",
      "notes": [
        "Field 的情节点一在第 20–30 分钟、二在第 80–90 分钟（按 120 分钟片）；各家页码和分钟数只是参考值。",
        "转折也可以是一场安静的决定戏，不一定是动作事件。"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plot_point",
        "https://sydfield.com/guest-blog/utilizing-syd-fields-screenwriting-paradigm-to-understand-script-timeline-structureby-natalia-lazarus/"
