      "zh": "机位",
      "en": "Camera setup",
      "zh_alt": "机位设置",
      "category": "delivery",
      "module": "影视改编",
      "def_zh": "拍一个镜头所需的物理布置：摄影机位置与运动、灯光、演员站位。重新架机或改灯算新机位。本剧没有实体机位，对应分镜 camera 里的机位描述。",
      "def_en": "The physical arrangement needed to film a shot: camera position and movement, lighting, actor marks. Moving the camera or relighting makes a new setup. In AI generation it maps to the camera description in the filming entry.",
      "where": "filming.json shots[].camera",
      "notes": [
        "只改演员走位通常算新的一条，不算新机位；两台机器同时拍是两个镜头、一个机位。"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://anonymousproductionassistant.com/2015/09/02/shots-versus-setups/"
      ],
      "in_graph": false,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "storyboard",
      "zh": "分镜",
      "en": "Storyboard / shot list",
      "zh_alt": "分镜头脚本、镜头表",
      "category": "artifact",
      "module": "影视改编",
      "def_zh": "把影片画面按镜头事先规划下来：分镜画出拍什么、为什么，镜头表列出每镜的角度、运动、景别与灯光。本剧的 filming.json 同时承担两者。",
      "def_en": "Pre-visualization of the film shot by shot: a storyboard illustrates what and why, a shot list specifies each shot's angle, movement, size and lighting. Our filming.json plays both roles.",
      "where": "episodes/epNN/filming.json",
      "notes": [
        "「分镜头脚本」在国内常指表格式文字分镜，更接近镜头表。"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://www.studiobinder.com/blog/shot-list-vs-storyboard/",
        "https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/分镜"
      ],
      "in_graph": false,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "master",
      "zh": "主镜头",
      "en": "Master shot",
      "zh_alt": "总镜头",
      "category": "shottype",
      "module": "影视改编",
      "def_zh": "从能看到所有人的角度，连续拍完整场戏的镜头，通常是远景、最先拍；其他覆盖都以它为剪辑基础。",
      "def_en": "A shot of an entire scene from start to finish, from an angle that keeps all actors in view; usually wide and filmed first, it anchors the rest of the coverage.",
      "where": "1.2.5.1 功能镜头",
      "notes": [
        "主镜头可以兼作建立镜头，建立镜头却不一定是主镜头。"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Master_shot"
      ],
      "in_graph": false,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "establishing",
      "zh": "建立镜头",
      "en": "Establishing shot",
      "zh_alt": "定场镜头",
      "category": "shottype",
      "module": "影视改编",
      "def_zh": "为接下来的场、段落或整部片交代环境，主要是地点，有时也交代时间；多为远景或航拍，让观众辨清方位。",
      "def_en": "A shot that sets up the context — mainly place, sometimes time — for the scene, sequence or film that follows; usually wide or aerial, it orients rather than engages emotionally.",
      "where": "1.2.5.1 功能镜头",
      "notes": [
        "长时间近景之后可再给一个「重新建立镜头」。"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://www.studiobinder.com/blog/what-is-an-establishing-shot-definition/"
      ],
      "in_graph": false,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "insert",
      "zh": "插入镜头",
      "en": "Insert shot",
